:: OC Jacob Intro 1 [nobr]

/* Intro */
You walk through the Arcade, browsing through the varies blinking and singing game cabinets trying to decide which experience you will spend your hard earned money on. Then, something catches your attention, <span style="color:Yellow">not a game but rather a small group who have gathered around one of the newly installed games.</span> HACK Brawlers Z Mayhem, quite the name and quite the machine. The fiery logo and theme music blaring would attract the attention of any young boy. But that’s not why they have gathered. <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "OC JACOB",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                    Eyes: "Mad",
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Gather round, gather round!”</span> A young boy about your age stands at the game, calling out to the small crowd. He has dark hair and a devious grin, a grin that makes you stop to listen. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That’s right, I’m announcing an open challenge! ‘<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span>’s Ultimate Gaming Tournament’! $10 buy-in, one epic match to decide the victor! Winner gets the pot, loser suffers the ultimate prank!”</span> The boy, who you guess is named <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span>, speaks with confidence and a touch of pride. Murmurs abound from the small crowd until one boy raises his hand. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What’s the ultimate prank?”</span> He asks. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m glad you asked!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span> smirks at this, widely. As if he was waiting for that question, to explain his master plan. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What’s a contest without a little risk? The ultimate loser will have to walk from here to the park in nothing but their underwear, supervised by the winner of course. Pretty good prank, if I say so myself.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span> smirks once more, fingers to his chin like he’s some genius on stage. <span style="color:Pink">It’s kind of cute.</span> <br>
<br>
The crowd, however, begins to murmur and disperse. You hear various reasonings. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah, not risking that.”</span> One kid laughs. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“$10 is all I have.”</span> Another one nervously states. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Obvious trap. Kid’s probably practiced a ton.”</span> A teenager chuckles. 

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "OC JACOB",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Wa- wait! Hold on a second! Cowards!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span> calls out, stepping down from the game’s platform as everyone starts to walk away. Soon, the entire crowd has dispersed outside of you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span>. He sighs, head down, shoulders slumped. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ryouta was right, maybe I should have only done $5.”</span> You can’t help but laugh, commenting that you don’t think the buy-in was the biggest problem. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span> pops up like a video game character as you speak, you could also see the exclamation point ding above his head. <span style="color:Yellow">His eyes lock with yours and you suddenly feel a little nervous.</span> He quickly slides over, smirk returning. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“So, one challenger remains, eh? You’re braver than the rest, aren’t you? I commend such courage!”</span> You raise an eyebrow, unsure if you actually want to risk embarrassment by playing against a kid who obviously considers himself very good at the game. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span> notices your hesitation and quickly tries to convince you. <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "OC JACOB",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                    Eyes: "Mad",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                    Eyes: "Tired",
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Don’t worry, I’m nothing if not fair! So, I’ll give you a handicap. You’ll get three lives and I’ll get one.”</span> You are surprised he would give you such a large handicap, though you are still unsure, <span style="color:Yellow">until <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span> looks up at you with pleading, desperate eyes.</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="Choice">
    <<link "Ask about the prank punishment<br>">>
    <<replace"#Choice">>
        You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span> why he chose to add a prank punishment to the tournament, especially one so embarrassing. That’s the part that seemed to scare most people off. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span> scoffs at your idea of having a tournament without a punishment. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Because it’s funny. And what’s a contest without a little risk? Won’t people play harder if they know something like that will happen if they lose?”</span> You admit he has a point, though still think his choice of prank is a bit too extreme for some. <br>
        <br>
        <<include"OC Jacob Intro 2">>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<link "Ask why he is doing this<br>">>
    <<replace"#Choice">>
        You ask him why he’s even doing this little contest and he blushes. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“For… fun?”</span> He tries to say, but you can tell that’s a lie. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright, alright. I MAY have spent next week’s lunch money on a new video game, but it’s not my fault! I HAD to have it! But I was hoping to get some of it back, so I didn’t have to survive off the kindness of friends for the next week.”</span> He laughs nervously, <span style="color:Pink">obviously a little embarrassed by his lack of willpower to not spend his food money on video games.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <<include"OC Jacob Intro 2">>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>

:: OC Jacob Intro 2 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 15>>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“So, what do you say? You get three lives, I get one. Are you in?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span> asks, putting his arm around you in a friendly manner in an attempt to persuade you. You’re still unsure if you want to risk the punishment, but the handicap is pretty good. You’d only need one lucky break to win. So, against your better judgement, you agree. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Perfect!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span> says evilly, his demeanor changing the instant you agree. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Then let the game begin!”</span> <br>
<br>
As you expected, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span> seems very familiar with this game. He instantly picks his character, a heroic looking boy named Harold, while you browse for a bit before deciding on your own, a cute lad named Kyle. You have no idea what his abilities or moves are, choosing simply on vibes alone. <span style="color:LightGreen">With your character selected, the battle begins!</span> <br>

