<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Player Two Wins!”</span> The game blares out <span style="color:LightGreen">as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span>, stunned, drops his controller. The boy is stunned for a moment, unable to believe that he lost. His brain tries to rationalize it, to come up with some trick that you used to win. But there was no trick, and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span>’s cheeks flush as he realizes this. He beat himself with his own confidence.</span> You nod, putting your controller down and taking the two $10 bills from the cabinet. You then turn to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jacob</span>, still stunned, and ask if he wants to back out of the punishment. This insult to his pride snaps him out of it. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Back out!? No way! I’m no coward!”</span> He proclaims, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You just got lucky, but I’m a boy of my word!”</span> He hesitates for a second before grabbing you by the arms, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“C- come on then! Let’s get this over with!”</span> <span style="color:Pink">He leads you outside to the populated streets as you can’t hide your excitement for what’s about to happen.</span> <br>
